      "text": "Rio de Janeiro to Manaus"
    },
    {
      "blockId": "tour:itinerary_text:5a4836cca1208c95",
      "field": "itinerary.text",
      "sourceTextSha256": "5bafa06f4b5d73d4453e0215dd80559041eed215cec5fc0d6f59e1470e340d59",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "ai_translation",
        "runId": "ada-en-20261109T2248-l2tuzoigvf",
        "model": "ChatGPT"
      },
      "text": "Fly to Manaus, the capital of Amazonas state and the main urban centre of the Brazilian Amazon. Your guide will meet you on arrival and take you to your hotel.\n\nThe rest of the day depends on your arrival time. If time allows, you can explore the city on your own.\n\nManaus grew particularly rapidly during the 19th-century rubber boom, when natural rubber was harvested from rubber trees in the Amazon rainforest. One of the most prominent landmarks of that era is the Amazonas Theatre, with its neoclassical architecture and colourful dome.\n\nOvernight in Manaus."
    },
